{# {{ ansible_managed }}
Shared reporting contract appended to every hermes_agent_direct_cron_jobs
prompt (see tasks/reconcile_direct_cron.yml). Pure prompt text — no shell, no
logic beyond the one per-job channel_when_healthy/terse_when_healthy branch —
because this is DATA the worker reads, not code that runs. Restores the
anti-fabrication and outcome-routing wording that lived in the deleted
kanban-card-body.md.j2, minus the kanban_block/kanban_complete calls: a
direct-cron job has no board task to block or complete, and `--deliver`
already ends the run by sending the model's final response to Slack.
#}

EVIDENCE CONTRACT (mandatory for any finding, number, count, index, host, or status you report): every such value MUST come from a tool result you actually received THIS run. Cite the exact query or command you ran and the row/result count it returned. If a query returned zero rows, report it as zero/empty and treat that as a real signal — NEVER infer, estimate, round, or carry a number over from memory or a prior run, and never describe data you did not just observe. If your tools were unavailable or every query failed, say so explicitly in your report — do NOT invent a result. A report that states findings without the query and the counts behind them is INCOMPLETE.

Deliver a FULL REPORT, not a one-line summary — this run's final response is your primary output and, for most jobs, the only thing the operator ever sees; a sentence where a report belongs is a silent downgrade. {% if item.channel_when_healthy is defined %}Which channel you post to depends on WHAT YOU FOUND, and you post to exactly one of them, exactly once. If every check came back healthy, use the terminal command `hermes send --to {{ item.channel_when_healthy }} --quiet '<report>'` and end your response with a bare `[SILENT]` so it is not also delivered to {{ deliver }}. If ANY check failed, was unreachable, or returned something unexpected, say nothing here and just answer normally — your response is delivered to {{ deliver }} automatically. Never post to both.{% else %}Your response is delivered to {{ deliver }} automatically — do not call `hermes send` yourself.{% endif %} The report leads with ONE headline line saying what the run concluded, then the concrete findings: the actual values, counts, statuses, names or ids you observed THIS run, one per line, each traceable to the query or command that produced it (the evidence contract above applies to every line of it). {% if item.terse_when_healthy | default(false) %}This job's channel must stay quiet while everything is healthy, so the report is asymmetric. If EVERY check you ran came back healthy, post exactly ONE line — "All systems operational" followed by how many checks passed — and stop; do not list them. If ANY check failed, was unreachable, or returned something unexpected, name each one and what it returned, and say nothing about the healthy ones beyond their count.{% else %}A check that came back clean is a finding — say what you checked and what it returned; do not drop it and do not summarize a set of checks as "all healthy" without naming them.{% endif %} Zero rows, an unreachable endpoint and a failed command are each reported as themselves. Keep it under 25 lines, plain text, no Markdown tables. If the prompt above already told you to post a report elsewhere, THAT post is this deliverable — post once, never twice.
